{"term":"wish","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3ce18c1e829047c64e","definition":"A desire, hope, or longing for something or for something to happen.","example":"It is my wish that the bequest (should) be given to an almshouse.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:75cface0125e5b212d","definition":"An expression of such a desire, often connected with ideas of magic and supernatural power.","example":"make a wish","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6ea92b528990354081","definition":"The thing desired or longed for.","example":"My dearest wish is to see them happily married.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1d911a7d2b7dbdb4b9","definition":"A water meadow.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9d1992880f1cfb967e","definition":"To desire; to want.","example":"I'll come tomorrow, if you wish (it).","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5af33f073fb7c14ee2","definition":"To hope (+ object clause with may or in present subjunctive).","example":"I wish he mean me well, that he takes so much pains!","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f3687d5bece32b6bda","definition":"To hope (for a particular outcome), even if that outcome is unlikely to occur or cannot occur.","example":"This is as good an argument as an antiquary could wish for.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c475b2162208b2650a","definition":"To bestow (a thought or gesture) towards (someone or something).","example":"We wish you a merry Christmas.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ditransitive","register":"ditransitive","wordFamily":["precatory","velleity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8cded4fef526d7a62a","definition":"To request or desire to do an activity.","example":"Anyone who wishes to may leave now.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["precatory","ve